Subject: [PATCH 06810/11362] wa30 L2 SOLVED: retract dead end, bank +1 level
 (69 -> 70)

A deliberate model-comparison probe (claude-fable-5, run fresh without
being told v1-v8's "infeasible" conclusion, only the confirmed
mechanics) found the mechanic all 9 prior attempts missed: an
unexplained color-12 glyph near the bay is a passive helper-robot NPC
that autonomously delivers blocks on any player action. This makes L2
a two-worker cooperative puzzle, not the single-worker puzzle v1-v8's
80-move lower bound assumed -- that math was correct but incomplete.

Before accepting this (a claim that directly overturns an
"exhaustively confirmed" dead end, and contradicts a separate
pre-session internal-state 40k-node search that also found nothing),
independently re-verified it rather than trusting the self-report:
extracted the artifact's 94-action sequence and ran
arc_solver_kit.reproduce() myself from 5 independent fresh
env.reset() calls using the project's existing wa30 apply()
convention (scripts/experiments/exp_headway_wa30.py). All 5 trials
returned reached_level=2, reproduced=True. The mechanical
arc-reproduced-count-integrity-lint also passes clean against the
updated counters.

levels_reproduced 1 -> 2 for wa30; reproducible_total_levels 69 -> 70.
No new GameAdapter yet -- this banks a frozen trajectory, not a
generalized solver; L3+ (same puzzle behind a barrier, per v9's
bonus recon) is future work.

